# GraphQL Conventions

## Layout (domain-colocated, mandatory)

GraphQL types and resolvers live under each feature's `graphql/` subfolder (see `nest-structure.mdc` for full module layout):

```
src/users/
  users.module.ts
  services/
    users.service.ts
  graphql/
    user.object.ts
    users.resolver.ts
    create-user.input.ts
```

Register the resolver as a provider in the feature module and import that module from `AppModule`. Do not use a `src/graphql/` folder or `GraphqlModule`.

## Naming

Use `<concept>.<role>.ts` — the concept answers *what*, the suffix answers *what role*:

```
graphql/
  auth.resolver.ts
  auth-payload.object.ts
  login-with-google.input.ts
  login-with-google.schema.ts
```

- Do **not** create generic container files (`auth.objects.ts`, `auth.inputs.ts`).
- Combine tightly related definitions in one file when they form a single contract.
- When a capability grows, split by subfolder (e.g. `graphql/sessions/`), not by artifact kind.

## Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ Object type (colocated with feature)
@ObjectType()
export class User {
  @Field(() => String)
  id!: string;

  @Field(() => String)
  email!: string;
}

// ✅ Input type for mutations
@InputType()
export class CreateUserInput {
  @Field(() => String)
  email!: string;
}

// ✅ Thin resolver — delegates to service
@Resolver(() => User)
export class UsersResolver {
  constructor(private readonly usersService: UsersService) {}

  @Query(() => User, { name: 'user', nullable: true })
  user(@Args('id', { type: () => String }) id: string) {
    return this.usersService.findById(id);
  }

  @Mutation(() => User, { name: 'createUser' })
  createUser(@Args('input') input: CreateUserInput) {
    return this.usersService.create(input);
  }
}

// ❌ Do not put Prisma queries directly in resolvers
```

## Validation

- Use Zod schemas colocated in `graphql/` (e.g. `login-with-google.schema.ts`) with the shared `parseInput()` helper.
- Keep Zod schemas next to their matching `@InputType` — they validate the same concept.

## Rules

- Use explicit `name` on `@Query` / `@Mutation` when it differs from the method name.
- Use `@Field(() => Type)` with explicit return types (avoid relying on reflection alone).
- Schema is generated to `src/generated/schema.gql` — never commit hand edits.
- GraphiQL / introspection: development only (see `GraphQLModule` config in `app.module.ts`).
- For guarded resolvers later, use `GqlExecutionContext` — not Express-only guards without GraphQL adaptation.
